### Proposed technology stack

| Layer                | Technology                                 |
| -------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |
| Language             | Kotlin                                     |
| UI                   | Jetpack Compose                            |
| Design               | Material foundations + custom Ucred system |
| Navigation           | Navigation Compose                         |
| State                | ViewModel + StateFlow                      |
| Local database       | Room                                       |
| Preferences          | DataStore                                  |
| Dependency injection | Hilt                                       |
| Backend              | Existing Firebase services, after audit    |
| Authentication       | Firebase Auth                              |
| Cloud database       | Cloud Firestore                            |
| AI processing        | Secure hosted backend                      |
| Camera               | CameraX                                    |
| Image processing     | ML Kit or existing verified OCR service    |
| Encryption           | Audited cryptographic implementation       |
| Build                | Gradle + Android Gradle Plugin             |

Exact dependency versions will be locked after checking compatibility during implementation.

### Backend and security rules

This is a critical migration area:

* Never embed Gemini API secrets in the APK.

* Keep privileged operations on a trusted backend.

* Preserve Firebase authentication rules.

* Verify Firestore security rules.

* Keep encryption keys out of plain-text preferences.

* Preserve guest vault functionality.

* Audit local encryption and backup recovery.

* Test account switching and data isolation.

The existing Next.js API routes cannot simply be assumed to work inside native Android. Their server-side responsibilities must remain hosted or be migrated to an appropriate backend.

