# UCRED — MASTER PROJECT RULES

## Product identity
Ucred is a premium, Apple-inspired Indian business finance operating system.

## Design direction
Ceramic surfaces, restrained frosted glass, spatial depth, premium typography, tactile native interactions and a distinctive Ucred visual identity.

## Technical direction
The final Android application must be implemented in Kotlin and Jetpack Compose. A WebView wrapper is not an acceptable substitute for the intended native application.

## Preservation rule
All existing business workflows, financial calculations, authentication, local storage, cloud sync, encryption, backup, receipt processing, billing and ledger features must be inventoried before migration. Do not remove or silently simplify any feature.

## Design rules
1. Use glass selectively.
2. Prioritise content clarity over decoration.
3. Use consistent spacing, typography and colour tokens.
4. Avoid unnecessary pills and floating cards.
5. Keep all financial figures readable.
6. Preserve accessible contrast and touch targets.
7. Support light and dark themes.
8. Use native, interruptible motion.
9. Respect reduced-motion preferences.
10. Never sacrifice performance for visual effects.

## Engineering rules
1. Keep UI, domain logic and data layers separate.
2. Keep secrets outside the APK.
3. Validate all financial calculations.
4. Preserve existing data semantics.
5. Implement explicit loading, empty, success and error states.
6. Test every important workflow.
7. Never claim completion without verification.

## Review rule
Every screen must pass visual review, interaction review, functional testing, accessibility checks and regression testing before being marked complete.

